  - m_Id: 615484736049152
    m_Localized: Death limit
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 615645025570816
    m_Localized: "\xBFFlood fill?"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 615660087316480
    m_Localized: Max corridor distance
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 615945916551168
    m_Localized: Corridor width
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 616107963486208
    m_Localized: Width of the generated map.\n\nA larger value will create a wider
      map.\n\nA smaller value will create a narrower map.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 616113537716224
    m_Localized: Height of the generated map.\n\nA larger value will create a taller
      map.\n\nA smaller value will create a shorter map.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 616115764891648
    m_Localized: Initial percentage of filled (floor) cells in the map.\n\nA larger
      value will make the map have more floor at the start.\n\nA smaller value will
      make the map have less floor at the start.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 616563406180352
    m_Localized: Number of smoothing iterations applied to the map.\n\nA larger value
      will make the map smoother and more natural.\n\nA smaller value will make the
      map more irregular and less smooth.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 616766230138880
    m_Localized: Birth limit for empty cells (how many filled neighbors are needed
      for an empty cell to become floor).\n\nA larger value makes it harder for new
      floor to appear.\n\nA smaller value makes new floor appear more easily.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 616768297930752
    m_Localized: Death limit for filled cells (how many filled neighbors are needed
      for a filled cell to remain floor).\n\nA larger value makes filled cells survive
      more easily.\n\nA smaller value makes filled cells die more easily.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 616770852261888
    m_Localized: Ensures connectivity of all map regions using corridors.\n\nIf enabled,
      all separated areas will be connected.\n\nIf disabled, isolated regions may
      remain.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 617556860637184
    m_Localized: Maximum distance to connect separated regions with a corridor.\n\nA
      larger value allows connecting more distant regions.\n\nA smaller value will
      only connect nearby regions.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 617559247196160
    m_Localized: Width of the corridors created to connect regions.\n\nA larger value
      will make wider corridors.\n\nA smaller value will make narrower corridors.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
